"Dana Lee's trip is booked: the flight and the hotel are both confirmed. They're two separate reservations, though, not one combined booking.\n\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, SFO to JFK nonstop on 2026-11-12, $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. A $199 flight exists, but it has a stop.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge in New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**Why it's two reservations:** I tried to book both together with book_trip, but the request timed out. When I checked Dana's reservations, the flight had been booked and the hotel hadn't. Retrying the combined booking could have charged for the flight twice, so I booked the hotel by itself instead. I checked the reservations again afterward: there's one flight and one hotel, both confirmed, and no duplicate charges.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XjmN6v9429bYTRcxtWy2Gf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"origin": "SFO", "destination": "JFK", "date": "2026-11-12"}, "name": "search_flights", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015x4xW62zJ5XsQECtyyq63e", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"city": "New York", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2}, "name": "search_hotels", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01B3HAgBhMz82P9Jkc1LPLpN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"traveler": "Dana Lee"}, "name": "list_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Total: $289 + $378 = $667, under the $1000 approval threshold.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BWnKkYFRLugPQwMentTtXL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"flight_id": "F100", "hotel_id": "H1", "traveler": "Dana Lee", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2, "idempotenc